Working through each unit against the semantic-linefeeds rule (one sentence per line; sub-splits only at real clause boundaries where both sides stand alone; `long` is advisory).

Unit 6 is the outlier: none of the 22 candidates fully separates all three fused sentences (every candidate either splits at an invalid point — the comma after the introductory "In order to create the dictionary entries," which isn't a recognized boundary — or leaves sentence 2 and sentence 3 still fused together). So I'm reporting a `missing` repair for that one.

