A few notes on the judgment calls:

- **Unit 1**: rejected every candidate that splits at "so it should have" — that fragment is truncated at the window edge and doesn't stand alone as a complete sentence, so `so` doesn't qualify as a coordinating boundary there.
- **Unit 6**: rejected all candidates because none resolves both sentence-fusion points (S1/S2 and S2/S3) correctly — most either sever the non-boundary intro comma after "entries," or leave S2 and S3 glued together on one line. My proposed repair does the mandatory one-sentence-per-line split and leaves each resulting long line alone, since `long` is advisory and none of the resulting sentences has a recognized clause boundary.
- **Units 4 & 8**: rejected candidates that split at intro adverbs ("Originally,", "Typically,", "In standard LSP,") since those aren't subordinators/relative pronouns and the split isn't needed for length either.
